.TH MBT 1 "2026-11-10" "Mojt Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mbt \- prepare private build tools and create Mojt build/package results
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mbt env
[--profile image|kernel] --source-manifest FILE --output DIRECTORY [--dry-run] [-y]
.PP
.B mbt build kernel
--plan FILE --config FILE --config-sha256 SHA256 --environment DIRECTORY
--output DIRECTORY [--source DIRECTORY] [--resume] [--jobs N] [--dry-run] [-y]
.PP
.B mbt package
{kernel|base|system|pack|verify} ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Experimental interface for review. MBT delegates to the existing environment,
Kernel build and native artifact tools. Use each command's --help for its flags.
No command installs a package, changes an active Ports profile, selects next
boot, replaces Base libc or changes a global compiler.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B env
Create a new private environment with pinned binary tools. The initial provider
is Nix; the tool inventory and library closure are retained beside the environment.
--dry-run previews without writing the environment or GC roots. No registry of
names or separate plan command is needed. Keep a created environment in place.
.TP
.B build kernel
Compile a separate versioned Kernel and matching modules as an ordinary user.
Source, configuration hash, policy and private environment remain explicit.
--dry-run validates inputs without fetching sources, compiling or writing output.
--resume requires the same verified inputs and an eligible incomplete workspace;
it does not repair arbitrary failed output. No automatic privilege escalation.
.TP
.B package
Create and independently verify a native archive from a complete build or
retained release. Packaging revision and original build provenance are distinct.
verify checks an existing archive without installing it. Packaging has no
--dry-run option in this initial interface; it writes a new explicit output.
.SH DELIVERY
Builder-enabled System images include the Python frontend, existing helper code,
this manual and a pinned Kernel recipe example. Compilers are acquired separately
in private environments. Ordinary System compositions need not carry MBT.
.SH LIMITS
Bootstrap, new-target image assembly and physical disk provisioning are not yet
joined to this frontend. There are no arbitrary recipes/hooks, saved-plan executor,
named-environment registry, GC or source rebuild of the entire distribution.
Runtime closure checks are not a universal libc/plugin compatibility guarantee.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpm (1)
